ORIGINAL AUTHOR AND METHOD

The original Photo Material Intervention workflow and its first three recipes
(Portal Woodcut, Paint-Stop Charcoal, and Sunlight Screenprint) were authored
and first publicly released by Pilipala9919 in 2026.

The method's identifying sequence is:

1. diagnose the photographic subject, strongest asset, real problem, goal, and fidelity risks;
2. choose the smallest effective route: hold, photographic edit, cleanup, narrative transformation, or material transformation;
3. require a source-specific meaning and—when social reach matters—a visible reason to stop or share before generation;
4. preserve truthful photographic anchors and separate genuine obstruction removal when needed;
5. use a strict default budget of one diagnosis, one strategy, one generation, and at most one local repair.

